<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{headline}}</title>
<!-- THE ACTIVE-CLIENT ALERT. The sibling grant-alert.hbs is the PROSPECT/LEAD one and
     keeps the how-to-get-started steps and the discovery-call booking link -- cold
     outreach to someone with no portal and no account manager needs both. A serviced
     client needs neither: the only thing we want from them is whether to pursue it.

     Brand fonts are embedded as local @font-face data URIs at render time (see
     lib/alerts/render.ts). No CDN <link>: serverless Chromium may have no egress to
     fonts.gstatic.com, and a competing/blocked CDN face is what garbled the glyphs.
     Design's mock specified Inter Tight / Source Serif 4; the embedded faces are the
     same two roles this template names, so the layout is the mock's and the type is
     ours. -->
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #e8e2d8; }
  @page { size: letter; margin: 0; }
  @media print {
    html { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
    html, body { background: #fff; }
    .brief-page { box-shadow: none !important; margin: 0 !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="brief-page" style="width:816px; min-height:1056px; margin:24px auto; padding:22px 0 0 0; background:#fff; color:#0B1E3A; font-family:'Inter Tight', sans-serif; box-shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(11,30,58,0.18); display:flex; flex-direction:column;">

  <!-- ===================== TOP BAR ===================== -->
  <!-- Mock (2026-09-15): logo + wordmark left, the tagline on the RIGHT (was the
       uppercase alertLabel). The alertLabel is dropped from the bar -- the orange
       kicker line under the rule already carries program/FON identity, so it was
       redundant. alertLabel stays in the data model for the email subject. -->
  <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; padding:0 46px;">
    <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:11px;">
      <img src="assets/granted-mark-navy.png" alt="GRANTED logo" width="31" height="31" style="display:block; flex-shrink:0;">
      <span style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-weight:700; font-size:23px; letter-spacing:0.04em; color:#0B1E3A;">GRANTED</span>
    </div>
    <span style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-style:italic; font-weight:700; font-size:14px; color:#0B1E3A;">More <span style="color:#E4761F; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:2px;">Grants</span>. Less Grind.</span>
  </div>

  <div style="height:1px; background:#0B1E3A; opacity:0.12; margin:14px 46px 0 46px;"></div>

  <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
  <!-- The chips moved UP here from their own section: on a client alert the fundable
       items are context for the description, not a section of their own. -->
  <div style="padding:18px 46px 14px 46px;">
    <!-- Title on the left, the FIT SCORE block on the right (client template only; the prospect teaser has
         no fit score). The number carries the signal and the word "Strong fit"/"Conditional"/"Weak" is
         redundant with it, so the block stays navy-neutral -- no band hue (the colour-blind rule). -->
    <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:space-between; gap:22px; margin-bottom:11px;">
      <div style="min-width:0;">
        <div style="font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.15em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#E4761F; margin-bottom:9px;">
          {{programName}}{{#if programShort}} &middot; {{programShort}}{{/if}}{{#if fiscalYear}} &middot; {{fiscalYear}}{{/if}}{{#if fon}} &middot; FON {{fon}}{{/if}}
        </div>
        <h1 style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-weight:700; font-size:37px; line-height:1.04; letter-spacing:-0.02em; margin:0; color:#0B1E3A;">
          {{headline}}
        </h1>
      </div>
      {{#if fitScore}}
      <div style="flex-shrink:0; text-align:center; border:1px solid rgba(11,30,58,0.14); border-radius:4px; padding:9px 16px 10px 16px;">
        <div style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-weight:700; font-size:32px; line-height:1; color:#0B1E3A;">{{fitScore}}</div>
        <div style="font-size:9px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#6E7683; margin-top:2px;">of 3</div>
        <div style="height:1px; background:rgba(11,30,58,0.1); margin:7px 0;"></div>
        <div style="font-size:8.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#6E7683;">Fit Score</div>
        <div style="font-size:11.5px; font-weight:700; color:#0B1E3A; margin-top:2px; white-space:nowrap;">{{fitScoreLabel}}</div>
      </div>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    <div style="font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.55; margin:0 0 11px 0; max-width:700px; color:#2a3a52; text-wrap:pretty;">{{{introHtml}}}{{#if statePassThrough}} In {{state}} it runs through the {{administeringAgency}} as a pass-through, so your application competes only against other in-state organizations, not the entire country.{{/if}}</div>
    {{#if whatItFunds.length}}
    <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:6px;">
      {{#each whatItFunds}}
      <span style="font-size:11.5px; font-weight:500; color:#0B1E3A; background:#faf7f2; border:1px solid rgba(11,30,58,0.12); border-radius:2px; padding:5px 9px;">{{this}}</span>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}
  </div>

  <!-- ===================== STATS STRIP ===================== -->
  <!-- Mock (2026-09-15): LIGHT tiles (white ground, navy serif numbers, grey labels)
       with a single ORANGE deadline tile (white text). The deadline tile also carries
       a middle "N days left" countdown (stat.sub, buildStats) between the date and the
       label -- absent when there's no firm future date. White-on-#E4761F matches the
       "Your call" button; the date value is large, so the tile's meaning is carried by
       the value + position, not the small label alone. -->
  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat({{stats.length}}, 1fr); margin:0 46px; border:1px solid rgba(11,30,58,0.12);">
    {{#each stats}}
    <div style="padding:12px 14px; {{#unless @last}}border-right:1px solid rgba(11,30,58,0.12); {{/unless}}display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; gap:3px; background:{{#if this.highlight}}#E4761F{{else}}#fff{{/if}};">
      <span style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-weight:700; font-size:21px; line-height:1; color:{{#if this.highlight}}#fff{{else}}#0B1E3A{{/if}}; max-width:100%; overflow:hidden; text-overflow:ellipsis; white-space:nowrap;">{{this.value}}</span>
      {{#if this.sub}}<span style="font-size:11px; font-weight:700; line-height:1; color:{{#if this.highlight}}#fff{{else}}#0B1E3A{{/if}};">{{this.sub}}</span>{{/if}}
      <span style="font-size:9.5px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.09em; text-transform:uppercase; color:{{#if this.highlight}}#fff{{else}}#6E7683{{/if}};">{{this.label}}</span>
    </div>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{#if statsFootnote}}
  <div style="font-size:10px; line-height:1.4; margin:6px 46px 0 46px; color:#6b7688;">{{statsFootnote}}</div>
  {{/if}}

  <!-- ============= WHO CAN APPLY, then GRANT INTELLIGENCE ============= -->
  <!-- Mock (2026-09-15): the two blocks are STACKED full-width, not the old side-by-side
       grid. "Who can apply" is a plain full-width paragraph directly under the stats
       strip; the "Grant Intelligence" read (resolveFit's narrative, swapped in for the
       old concept synopsis) is the full-width orange-left-border callout below it.

       Full-width means the callout sizes to its content -- no min-height prop is needed
       to keep it from reading as a small box adrift in a column (that was a two-up-grid
       problem). grantIntelligence is still clamped in buildAlertData (GRANT_INTEL_MAX) so
       a long narrative can't drive the page past one letter sheet and push the decision
       band off the bottom. The band stays pinned to the bottom by margin-top:auto below;
       whatever slack a short alert leaves lands above it, the shape of a one-page letter. -->
  <div style="padding:14px 46px 2px 46px;">
    <div style="font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#E4761F; margin-bottom:9px;">Who can apply</div>
    <p style="font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.55; margin:0; color:#2a3a52;">{{{eligibilityHtml}}}</p>
    {{#if eligibilityNote}}
    <div style="background:#faf7f2; border-left:3px solid #E4761F; padding:10px 12px; margin-top:10px;">
      <div style="font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#E4761F; margin-bottom:3px;">{{eligibilityNote.label}}</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px; line-height:1.45; color:#2a3a52;">{{eligibilityNote.body}}</div>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    <div style="background:#faf7f2; border-left:3px solid #E4761F; padding:16px 18px; margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#E4761F; margin-bottom:10px;">Grant Intelligence</div>
      <p style="font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.6; margin:0; color:#2a3a52; text-wrap:pretty;">{{#if grantIntelligence}}{{grantIntelligence}}{{else}}We will scope how your organization would run this programme once you tell us to proceed.{{/if}}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================== YOUR CALL ===================== -->
  <!-- ONE reliable way through, not two one-click buttons. A PDF's links are not
       dependable where most people first open the attachment -- Gmail's preview pane
       (especially on mobile) frequently does not activate them, and a control that
       looks pressable but is not is the dead affordance this product keeps removing.
       A PDF also cannot show what you already clicked, and it gets DOWNLOADED, so a
       decision token would sit in a Downloads folder indefinitely.
       So one-click lives in the EMAIL (see lib/email/html.ts DecisionBox) and this
       carries a portal deep link: honest in every viewer, still readable when printed,
       and it lands a forwarded reader on login rather than on someone else's decision.
       No booking link -- that is prospect-shaped, and an active client has an account
       manager rather than a discovery call to schedule.

       margin-top:auto ONLY. With margin-bottom:auto as well, a flex item takes ALL the
       page's leftover height and splits it evenly above and below itself -- so a short
       alert opened two gaps instead of none: one under the concept grid, and a dead white
       strip between this navy band and the footer, which read as a rendering fault. The
       page is min-height:1056px and the content rarely fills it, so that slack has to land
       somewhere; the only question is where. Top-only sends all of it above the band,
       which pins the band and the footer together at the bottom of the letter page -- the
       normal shape for a one-page document, and it keeps the closing rule flush against
       the footer at every content length. -->
  <div style="margin-top:auto; padding:0;">
    <div style="height:3px; background:#E4761F;"></div>
    <div style="background:#0B1E3A; color:#faf7f2; padding:22px 46px 20px 46px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.25fr 1fr; gap:34px; align-items:center;">
      <div>
        <div style="font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.13em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#e6b89a; margin-bottom:7px;">Your call</div>
        <p style="font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.55; margin:0 0 8px 0; color:#e2e9f2; text-wrap:pretty;">Tell us how to proceed. <b style="color:#fff;">Interested</b> moves this into your grant report for full analysis; <b style="color:#fff;">Pass</b> clears it off your list.</p>
        <div style="font-size:10.5px; line-height:1.45; color:#adbcd0;">You can answer in one click straight from the alert email, or just reply to it. Not ready this cycle? Pass and we position you for the next one.</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        {{#if portalUrl}}
        <a href="{{portalUrl}}" style="display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:10px; background:#E4761F; color:#fff; text-decoration:none; padding:13px 16px; border-radius:3px;">
          <span style="font-size:14px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.01em;">Review and decide in your portal</span>
          <span style="font-size:16px; line-height:1;">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
        {{else}}
        <div style="border:1px solid rgba(250,247,242,0.35); border-radius:3px; padding:13px 16px; font-size:13px; line-height:1.45; color:#cdd6e2;">Answer from the alert email, or reply to it and we will record your decision.</div>
        {{/if}}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="height:3px; background:#E4761F;"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ===================== FOOTER ===================== -->
  <!-- Light and compact, replacing the prospect footer's navy block and firm blurb. A
       client does not need to be told who we are. -->
  <div style="height:1px; background:#0B1E3A; opacity:0.12; margin:0 46px;"></div>
  <div style="background:#fff; color:#0B1E3A; padding:14px 46px 16px 46px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:30px;">
    <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px;">
      <img src="assets/granted-mark-navy.png" alt="GRANTED logo" width="27" height="27" style="display:block; flex-shrink:0;">
      <span style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-weight:700; font-size:18px; letter-spacing:0.03em; color:#0B1E3A;">GRANTED</span>
      <span style="font-family:'Source Serif 4', serif; font-style:italic; font-size:14px; color:#E4761F;">More Grants. Less Grind.</span>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px;">
      <span style="font-size:12.5px; font-weight:600; color:#0B1E3A;">grantedco.com</span>
      <span style="width:1px; height:13px; background:rgba(11,30,58,0.2); display:inline-block;"></span>
      <span style="font-size:12.5px; font-weight:500; color:#E4761F;">support@grantedco.com</span>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
